<title>USA: N.Y. business loans fell $151 mln September 25 wk. [CORRECTED 22:05 GMT]</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans fell $151 mln September 25 wk. [CORRECTED 22:05 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six (corrects from seven) major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $157 million to $42.010 billion in the week ended September 25, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $151 million to $42.260 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $8.416 billion to $748.171 billion.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
